{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Now I know that YHWH is greater than all the elohim, for in the very matter in which they dealt presumptuously against them.</b> He says that he recognized the preeminence of the God of Israel and His greatness above all the elohim, בדבר אשר זדו — that is, in that He repaid them measure for measure for the presumptuousness (זדון) which they practiced against them. The intention is that had they not dealt presumptuously against them, He would not have punished them, because they were fulfilling His decree, as He said (Genesis 15:13): ״ועבדום וענו אותם״. But what they added beyond what was decreed, in that they said (Exodus 1:22): ״כל הבן הילוד היאורה תשליכוהו״ and so forth — this is uprooting; it is not included in the category of servitude and affliction. Upon this addition the punishment came. And the reason he added the word כי and said כי בדבר is to explain that He punished them בדבר אשר זדו; and so it is written in the book of Ezra (Nehemiah 9:10): ״כי ידעת כי הזידו עליהם״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:39.368348564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}